--- A tool only handed to a model — never called by the program — is typed
--- by what its body reads (spec, Tools are the functions): `upper[x]`
--- reads its parameter as text, and the schema the compiler writes says
--- so. Only a call had typed one, and a tool read in its body was refused
--- as typed by nothing, the refusal's own fix ("read it in the body")
--- doing nothing. (The model's address answers nobody: the call's failure
--- is the same value in both modes.)
use llm

--- says its argument back, louder
fn shout[x]
    return upper[x]

m = reach['openai://127.0.0.1:9/self-model']
r = chat[m, ask['hi'], tools = [shout]]
log[r.ok]
log[r.kind]
